     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order yet because the dose needs to be checked first.\n\n**The problem:** Metformin 1700 mg three times daily adds up to **5100 mg/day**. That's about twice the labeled maximum:\n- Immediate-release metformin: max **2550 mg/day**\n- Extended-release metformin: max **2000 mg/day**\n\nDoses this high raise the risk of lactic acidosis and serious GI side effects, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\n**This may be a transcription error.** Common regimens close to what you wrote are:\n1. **Metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2550 mg/day, the IR maximum)\n2. **Metformin 1700 mg/day total**, given as 850 mg PO twice daily with meals\n3. **Metformin 1000 mg PO twice daily with meals** (2000 mg/day, a common target dose)\n\nPlease tell me which regimen you meant, and whether it's immediate- or extended-release, and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and give a brief clinical reason. I'll add a note to the order saying it's above the labeled maximum, and pharmacy will likely review it too."
      }
     ],
